# Anthropic — egress this entry needs.
#
# Allowlist syntax, so what you read here is what lands in the deployment's
# /etc/agent-allowlist. Uncommented lines are what the provider needs to work;
# anything below the OPTIONAL marker is off until you turn it on.
#
# METHODS is not optional in practice. Omitting it defaults the entry to
# GET,HEAD,OPTIONS, and every request Claude Code makes is a POST — so a bare
# `api.anthropic.com` line blocks the provider completely while looking right.

api.anthropic.com       GET,POST

# GET is here for model listing (GET /v1/models), which some clients call at
# startup; POST carries /v1/messages and /v1/messages/count_tokens. Narrowing
# to POST alone is safe for Claude Code itself and is the tighter choice if you
# know your client never lists models. Widening past these two is not needed by
# anything: the Admin API under /v1/organizations is refused by the addon
# regardless of what this file says.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL — nothing below is needed for the provider to work.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# statsig.anthropic.com   POST    # feature flags; the client works without it
# sentry.io               POST    # error reporting
#
# Note what these are NOT: they belong in an allowlist and must never appear in
# the entry's `hosts`. `hosts` is where the addon attaches the Anthropic
# credential, and attaching it to a Sentry request is exactly the accident the
# addon's host matching exists to prevent. Reachable and credentialed are two
# different lists that happen to overlap.
